# Not needed by `next build` — keeps the deploy upload small (the audit
# docs alone are ~10MB, and large uploads have flaked on this network).
# Patterns are root-anchored: a bare "supabase" would also exclude
# lib/supabase/ (gitignore semantics) and break the build.
/docs
/out
/supabase

# NOT /scripts. The build script now chains scripts/verify-static.mjs, which
# fails the deploy if the marketing routes stop being prerendered — excluding
# the directory would make every Vercel build die on a missing module. The
# whole directory is 144 KB; the upload savings this was buying were noise
# next to /docs.

# 9.7MB of graphify knowledge-graph output. Not gitignored historically, so
# it would otherwise be uploaded on every `vercel --prod` from a working copy.
/graphify-out
